Rule 1 (input tensor must have at least one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor must have a numeric, boolean, or complex data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor has complex floating-point data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10
>>
Rule 4 (input tensor has at least one dimension and all dimensions are non-empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 5 (multi-dimensional input tensor has positive size along the last axis)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) > 0
>>
Rule 6 (input tensor has a real integer or floating-point data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 7 (input tensor is 1-dimensional with positive length)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 8 (input tensor has at least two elements along the last axis)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 9 (input tensor is 2-dimensional with positive dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0
>>
Rule 10 (non-complex input tensor must have an upcastable boolean, integer, or floating-point data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10 then dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
